<http://data.silknow.org/object/a84736b3-591d-31f3-8a55-7948352be604/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "In the 18th century, women’s stays served to mould the torso to the fashionable shape and provide a rigid form on which the gown could be arranged and fastened. Because they were underwear and therefore never seen, stays were usually made of plain linen, but this example provides a colourful and luxurious alternative."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a84736b3-591d-31f3-8a55-7948352be604> .

